text:
Race condition. Multiple requests read same value before any write commit.

## Fix options

**1. Atomic update (best)**
```sql
UPDATE counters
SET value = value + 1
WHERE id = $1
RETURNING value;
```
DB handle increment atomically. No read-then-write in app code.

**2. Row-level lock**
```sql
BEGIN;
SELECT value FROM counters WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE;
UPDATE counters SET value = value + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING value;
COMMIT;
```
`FOR UPDATE` blocks other reads until tx done. Slower under load.

**3. Advisory lock** — overkill here. Skip.

## Node code (option 1)

```js
app.post('/counter/increment', async (req, res) => {
  const { rows } = await pool.query(
    'UPDATE counters SET value = value + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING value',
    [req.params.id]
  );
  res.json({ value: rows[0].value });
});
```

## Why this works

`UPDATE` in Postgres = atomic read+write at DB level. Concurrent requests queue at DB, each get unique incremented value.

**Use option 1.** Atomic update solve problem in one query, no tx overhead.
